/F1 10.5 Tf (Nordic Appliance Care - Salesforce Field Service Requirements) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (Version 1.2 - Prepared for the implementation partner) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf () Tj T*
/F1 15 Tf (1. Background) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (Nordic Appliance Care repairs household appliances across Sweden and Norway. Today) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (technicians receive jobs by phone and paper, and customers have no visibility of when a) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (technician will arrive. The company wants to run its service operation on Salesforce Field) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (Service.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf () Tj T*
/F1 15 Tf (2. Work Order Management) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (2.1 Work order intake) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Customer service agents must create a work order from a case in one click, copying the) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (customer, address and appliance.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Every work order must have a priority \(Low, Medium, High, Critical\) derived from the) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (appliance warranty status.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Work orders created outside business hours should be flagged for next-day dispatch.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (2.2 Scheduling and dispatch) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Dispatchers must see all unscheduled work orders on the Gantt and schedule them to) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (technicians by skill and territory.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- The system shall send the customer an SMS with the arrival window when an appointment is) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (dispatched.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Appointments must not be scheduled outside the technician's working hours.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf () Tj T*
/F1 15 Tf (3. Mobile Technician Experience) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Technicians must be able to view the job, appliance history and parts list offline in the) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (Field Service mobile app.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Technicians shall capture the customer signature and photos before completing a job.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- When a job cannot be completed the technician must select a reason and the system should) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (create a follow-up appointment.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf () Tj T*
/F1 15 Tf (4. Data Migration) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- All active customers \(approx. 60,000\) and their appliances must be migrated from the) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (legacy ServiceMax system.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Open work orders and the last 24 months of service history shall be migrated with their) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (original reference numbers.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Duplicate customers must be merged before go-live. Matching rules are TBD with the data) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (owner.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf () Tj T*
/F1 15 Tf (5. Integrations) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Spare parts stock must be checked in real time against the SAP warehouse API before a part) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (is reserved.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Completed work orders shall be sent to SAP for invoicing within 15 minutes.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- If SAP is unavailable the integration must retry and alert the support team.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf () Tj T*
/F1 15 Tf (6. Reporting) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Service managers need a dashboard with first-time fix rate, average travel time and SLA) Tj T*
ET
